    {
      "extracted_at": "2026-10-14T01:10:04Z",
      "payload": {
        "chunks": [
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "NOTE 4",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "the Data Center segment, which primarily includes Artificial Intelligence (AI) accelerators, server microprocessors (CPUs), graphics processing units (GPUs), accelerated processing units (APUs), data processing units (DPUs), Field Programmable Gate Arrays (FPGAs), Smart Network Interface Cards (SmartNICs) and Adaptive System-on-Chip (SoC) products for data centers;",
            "entity_name": "AMD Data Center Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "NOTE 4",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "the Client segment, which primarily includes CPUs, APUs, and chipsets for desktops and notebooks;",
            "entity_name": "AMD Client Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "NOTE 4",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "the Gaming segment, which primarily includes discrete GPUs, and semi-custom SoC products and development services;",
            "entity_name": "AMD Gaming Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "NOTE 4",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "the Embedded segment, which primarily includes embedded CPUs, GPUs, APUs, FPGAs, System on Modules (SOMs), and Adaptive SoC products.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Embedded Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "NOTE 5",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "On August 9, 2024, the Company completed the acquisition of Silo AI Oy (Silo AI), an AI lab based in Finland in an all-cash transaction of $665 million. Net of closing adjustments, transaction costs and deferred cash compensation, the purchase consideration of $553 million was allocated to $19 million of identifiable intangible assets, $43 million of net liabilities assumed, and $577 million to goodwill.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Acquisition of Silo AI Oy",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "NOTE 5",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "On August 17, 2024, the Company entered into an agreement (the Agreement) to acquire ZT Group Int'l, Inc. (ZT Systems), a provider of AI and general purpose compute infrastructure for hyperscale computing companies, in a cash and stock transaction valued at approximately $4.9 billion (the Acquisition). The aggregate closing consideration payable by the Company consists of 8,335,852 shares of the Company's common stock and $3.4 billion in cash. The Acquisition is expected to close in the first half of 2025, subject to certain regulatory approvals and other customary closing conditions.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Pending Acquisition of ZT Systems",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Consolidated Statements of Operations",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "Restructuring charges\n\n186 — — ",
            "entity_name": "AMD 2024 Restructuring Plan",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "NOTE 6",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "During the fourth quarter of fiscal year 2024, the Company determined that the fair value of certain IPR&D recorded within the Data Center segment was not recoverable resulting from actions related to the 2024 Restructuring Plan, and recorded an impairment charge of $58 million within Restructuring charges in the Company's Consolidated Statement of Operations.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Data Center IPR&D Impairment Q4 2024",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "NOTE 2",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In November 2023, the Financial Accounting Standards Board (FASB) issued Accounting Standard Update (ASU) 2023-07 Segment Reporting (Topic 280) Improvements to Reportable Segment Disclosures to enhance disclosures about significant segment expenses. This ASU is effective for the Company's fiscal year 2024 and interim periods in fiscal year 2025. The Company adopted this standard in the fourth quarter of 2024.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Adoption of ASU 2023-07 Segment Reporting",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_return",
            "content": "Repurchases of common stock(862)(985)(3,702)",
            "entity_name": "AMD FY2024 Common Stock Repurchases",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalReturn",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "NOTE 8",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_structure_event",
            "content": "The 2.95% Notes with a principal amount of $750 million were repaid in June 2024.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Repayment of 2.950% Senior Notes Due 2024",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalStructureEvent",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "NOTE 8",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "esg_commitment",
            "content": "The Revolving Credit Agreement also contains a sustainability-linked pricing component which provides for interest rate and facility fee reductions or increases based on the Company meeting or missing targets related to environmental sustainability, specifically greenhouse gas emissions.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Sustainability-Linked Revolving Credit GHG Pricing",
            "entity_type_entity": "ESGCommitment",
            "valid_from": "2025-01-28",
            "valid_until": null
          }
        ],
